        "evidence_id": "E001",
        "passage_id": "P001",
        "quote": "Appeal from an order of the Supreme Court, Niagara County (Matthew J. Murphy, III, A.J.), entered October 29, 2019. The order granted the motion of defendants for summary judgment dismissing the complaint.",
        "statement_status": "procedural_history"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E002",
        "passage_id": "P001",
        "quote": "It is hereby ordered that the order so appealed from is unanimously reversed on the law without costs, the motion is denied, and the complaint is reinstated.",
        "statement_status": "current_disposition"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E003",
        "passage_id": "P001",
        "quote": "Memorandum: Plaintiff commenced this action seeking damages for injuries she allegedly sustained when she slipped and fell on snow and ice on defendants' property.",
        "statement_status": "allegation"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E004",
        "passage_id": "P002",
        "quote": "Assuming, arguendo, that the report of defendants' expert meteorologist was sufficient to establish that there was a storm at the location where plaintiff fell ( cf. Ayers v Pioneer Cent. Sch. Dist. , 187 AD3d 1625 , 1625 [4th Dept 2020]), we conclude that defendants failed to meet their initial burden of establishing that \"plaintiff's injuries [were] sustained as the result of any icy condition occurring during an ongoing storm or for a reasonable time thereafter\"",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E005",
        "passage_id": "P003",
        "quote": "In support of their motion, defendants submitted the deposition testimony of plaintiff, who testified that it had snowed the night before the accident, but that it was not snowing at the time of her fall at 10:00 a.m. on the day of the accident. Plaintiff further testified that, while the sidewalks and ramp to the staircase of defendants' building had been cleared of snow, the steps were still snow-covered.",
        "statement_status": "testimony_or_record"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E006",
        "passage_id": "P002",
        "quote": "We agree with plaintiff that Supreme Court erred in granting defendants' motion for summary judgment dismissing the complaint.",
